e deterministic provider double injected at the same seam production uses, process-spawned CLI tests under `LHC_PROCESS_SUITE=1`.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/02-derivation-pipeline/artifacts/05-message-edit-cascade/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:196:**SDK construction in tests:** `createSdk({ provider: double, mode: \"manual\", retry: { budget: 3, backoffBaseMs: 0, backoffCapMs: 0 }, lease: { durationMs: 200 } })` unless a test says otherwise. Background-mode tests construct with `mode: \"background\"` and await `drainSettled`. Spawned CLI process tests set `LHC_PROVIDER` to the deterministic provider registered through the same named-provider registry production uses; no spawned test injects a provider through a test-only path.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/02-derivation-pipeline/artifacts/05-message-edit-cascade/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:217:### `cli-process-work.test.ts` — Flow 1 (spawned processes, `LHC_PROCESS_SUITE=1`)\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/02-derivation-pipeline/artifacts/05-message-edit-cascade/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:283:CLI parity legs of TC-5.6/TC-6.8 live in `cli-process-work.test.ts` alongside the other spawned tests.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/02-derivation-pipeline/artifacts/05-message-edit-cascade/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:289:**Story 0 — versioned work-item ids (DD-1/DD-3).** Ids gain the source-version suffix: `w-t1-turn_derivation` → `w-t1-turn_derivation-v1`. Every exact-id assertion in Epic 01 suites updates accordingly — known sites: `test/work-queue.test.ts` (~8 `workItemId:` literals), `test/cli-process-work-queue.test.ts` (2). Sweep `\"w-` literals during Story 0 red phase and list each in the deviation table.\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/02-derivation-pipeline/artifacts/05-message-edit-cascade/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:359:      - \"packages/lhc/test/cli-process-mutations.test.ts\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/02-derivation-pipeline/artifacts/05-message-edit-cascade/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:373:        - \"TC-5.1 through TC-5.6 remain covered by mutations.test.ts and cli-process-mutations.test.ts from initial verification; focused test suites pass after the fix.\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/02-derivation-pipeline/artifacts/05-message-edit-cascade/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:375:        - \"LHC_PROCESS_SUITE=1 pnpm vitest run test/cli-process-mutations.test.ts passed: 2 tests.\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/02-derivation-pipeline/artifacts/05-message-edit-cascade/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:385:        command: \"LHC_PROCESS_SUITE=1 pnpm vitest run test/cli-process-mutations.test.ts\"\npackages/lhc/docs/02-specs/02-derivation-pipeline/artifacts/05-message-edit-cascade/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:441:    planSummary: \"Implemented Story 5 (message edit and cascade): a new shared cascade module (src/domains/messages/internal/cascade.ts) derives the clear-set structurally from the message → turn → chunk walk over existing derived_form rows, supersede-deletes still-queued old-version items (reported on the result), and enqueues replacements at each group's max source version + 1 inside the mutation's transaction. messages.edit validates through the deleted-filtered read (turn_open / message_not_found refusals), applies content + blocks + token re-stamp via new store.ts helpers (readMutableMessage / applyMessageEdit mirroring projectEvent's counted fields), runs the cascade, and returns the MutationResult — one synchronous commit, with enqueue pokes riding onCommit so background mode rebuilds with no further call. The source-version check (existing single write path in work-queue complete()) is provoked by TC-5.4's delayed-double recipe: a real claimed pre-edit item held across the edit completes after the post-edit replacement is queued and discards as stale_discarded. CLI: new src/cli/messages-mutate.ts and `lhc messages edit --message/--message-id --content` 